senses.gloss:
मत्वा, ind. having thought; having believed;
having considered; having known or understood;
having remembered.

मातय (fr. मातृ), Nom. P. मातयति, &c.;
अममातत् = मातरम् आख्यत्, Schol. on Pāṇ. VII.
4, 2.

मात्रक = मात्र at the end of comps. (e. g.
छाया-मात्रक, lasting only as long as a shadow;
मन्त्र-ब्राह्मण-मात्रकात्, from the Mantras
and Brāhmaṇas alone; जात-मात्रक, just born);
(इका), f. = मात्रा, the prosodial time of a short
vowel, &c.
